  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Tied through six innings until Grisham broke it open in the seventh.",
    "what_this_means": "Baltimore came to hold, but late-inning baseball is where this lineup still finds its weight. Grisham's three-run night mattered because runners were already on base. The offense had moved pieces into position, and he converted them. Rod\u00f3n gave them four clean innings, and the bullpen did not blink: De los Santos worked two scoreless, and Bednar closed it out. Two runs in the seventh, one run held from the eighth on. That is the math of 70-55. They're five back now because they stopped folding when it would have been easy to fold. This team doesn't lose one-run games by accident anymore.",
